  "adaptations": [
    "The uploaded concept is the visual target, not a claim that the underlying synthesizer supports arbitrary modular cable rewiring. The routing selector exposes Surge's real eight routing configurations.",
    "The routing canvas uses the reference's node geometry. Native menus inside oscillator, filter and effect nodes, mixer faders, and the right-hand parameter inspector control actual engine parameters.",
    "The inspector promotes Filter 1 while its lower knob row also exposes Filter 2 cutoff/resonance; this replaces the concept's redundant velocity/keytrack row and keeps both filters immediately editable.",
    "All eight macros are bound to the processor. Their actual names and current values replace reference-only labels and fabricated readouts.",
    "Eight real FX algorithm selectors occupy the displayed chain. Remaining native slots and detailed effect parameters stay available through Full editor.",
    "The plot is a qualified filter-response preview. Output meters reflect actual signal levels, and the full native oscilloscope is available through Open scope.",
    "The header uses functioning preset navigation, Scene A/B, skin selection and Full editor access. Exact generated logos, miniature icons, and inert concept tabs are not reproduced as fake controls.",
    "The modulation panel reports native patch routes; route creation and detailed editing use the existing modulation editor.",
    "These are native vector controls and labels, not an image pasted over the synth. Pixel-identical photographic materials, illustration details and impossible generated labels are not claimed."
  ]
}
